# MythosMUD Stacked PRs (gh-stack)

When shipping MythosMUD work through GitHub, **prefer `gh stack`** over ad-hoc
`git push` + `gh pr create` whenever more than one logical layer exists, or the
current branch already belongs to a stack.

## Apply skill

Read and follow `.cursor/skills/gh-stack/SKILL.md` (full command reference:
`.agents/skills/gh-stack/SKILL.md`).

## When to use stacks (automatic)

| Situation                                                           | Action                                                                          |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Large change with dependency layers (models → API → client → tests) | Plan layers; `gh stack init` / `add` per layer                                  |
| Open / update PRs for stacked work                                  | `gh stack submit --auto` (add `--open` when ready for review)                   |
| Sync after trunk or base PR merged                                  | `gh stack sync` (add `--prune` to drop merged local branches)                   |
| Mid-stack fix needed while on a higher branch                       | `gh stack down` / `checkout` lower layer → commit → `gh stack rebase --upstack` |
| Merge stacked PRs                                                   | `gh stack merge --yes` (not `gh pr merge` alone)                                |
| Single small independent PR                                         | Plain `gh pr create` is fine                                                    |

## Non-interactive agent rules (hard)

- Always `gh stack view --json` (never bare `view` / TUI).
- Always `gh stack submit --auto`.
- Always pass branch names to `init`, `add`, `checkout`.
- Prefer `--remote origin` on `push` / `submit` / `sync` / `rebase` when useful.
- Do **not** change `git config` unless the user explicitly asks (user policy).
  If prompts appear for remotes, pass `--remote origin` instead.
- Commits: standard `git add` / `git commit` (Mythos commit-message skill); then stack tools for push/PR.
- Branch switches still need user permission when they leave the approved task branch; stack
  `up` / `down` / `top` / `bottom` within an already-approved stack for this task is OK.

## Session hygiene

On PR-related work, run `gh stack view --json` early. If exit code 2 (not in a stack)
and the user wants stacked PR(s), `gh stack init <branch...>` with explicit names
(or adopt the current branch: `gh stack init $(git branch --show-current)`).
